    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "UDMA CRC errors (UAS bridge health)",
      "description": "CRC errors accumulate on the LINK between host and disk \u2014 cable, bridge, controller \u2014 not on the platters. On this host that makes them the leading indicator that the OWC/UAS enclosure is degrading: they climb before the abort storm that drops the tank pool. See project_tank_uas_enclosure_failure. Alert: SmartUDMACRCErrorsRising on any increase over 6h.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 7
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": true,
            "axisPlacement": "auto",
            "gradientMode": "opacity"
          },
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true,
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "smartctl_device_attribute{attribute_name=\"UDMA_CRC_Error_Count\",attribute_value_type=\"raw\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{device}}",
          "range": true,
          "instant": false,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Bad-sector counters",
      "description": "Media defects on the platters. These are REACTIVE: they only move once the drive has already tripped over a bad sector during real I/O, which is exactly why scheduled self-tests matter \u2014 an extended test reads the whole surface and finds latent defects in cold data first. Alerts: SmartReallocatedSectors, SmartPendingSectors.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 7
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
